blocks.en:
Metrics. We evaluate pose reconstruction using five metrics commonly reported in sparse inertial motion capture [ 24 , 23 ] :
1) SIP error , the average global rotation discrepancy for the upper arms and thighs;
2) angular error (Ang) , the corresponding average across all joints;
3) position error (Pos) , the average distance between predicted and ground-truth joint positions relative to the root;
4) mesh error , the average distance between corresponding SMPL vertices after root-position alignment; and
5) jitter , the average magnitude of the third temporal derivative of predicted joint positions.
Setup recovery is evaluated using
6) recovery time , the time until all assignments are correct and mean mounting error falls below a specified threshold; and
7) mounting error , the geodesic distance between estimated and true mounting rotations.

blocks.zh:
度量衡. 我们使用通常在稀有惯性运动捕捉中报告的5个度量值来评估重建情况[24,23]:
(1) SIP出错,上臂和大腿平均全球自转差异;
2) 角误差(Ang),所有关节的相应平均值;
3) 位置错误(Pos),相对于根部的预测和地-地-地联合位置之间的平均距离;
4)网格错误,在根位对齐后对应的 SMPL 顶点之间的平均距离;以及
5),预测联合位置的第三个时间衍生物的平均规模.
使用
6) 恢复时间,直至所有任务都正确并意味着上升错误低于规定的阈值;以及
7) 上升出错,估计与真实上升旋转之间的大地测量距离。
